  "$comment": "The order each release lists its drawings in, read off the Figma Changelog page on 9 Sep 2026 and pinned here so the site and the Paper board print the same sequence. Some entries are hand-ordered by family (0.6.0 opens on the singles and walks the money through its bases and circled halves) and some are plain alphabetical; which is which is the design file's call, not this file's. A name missing from a version's list is not dropped: build-history.mjs appends it in its own order and says so, so an entry can never publish fewer drawings than the release contained. 0.3.0 is deliberately absent: that entry adds no drawings, and the row of thirty under it is the sharp sample, which is named in lib/changelog.ts and already matches. Read by pipeline/build-history.mjs.",
